        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "policy: classify doctor fix recommendations",
        "body": "## Summary\n\n- add policy doctor fix metadata covering every current policy finding\n- classify findings as `automatic`, `reviewRequired`, `manual`, `validateOnly`, or `unsupported`\n- attach structured `fixRecommendation` data to emitted policy findings without changing `doctor --fix`\n- emit `fixRecommendation` through both `policy check --json` and `doctor --lint --json`\n- keep policy attestation payloads stable by leaving recommendation metadata out of attested findings / attestation hashes\n- add metadata/tests that fail when a policy check id lacks a fix classification\n\n## Validation\n\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs extensions/policy/src/doctor/metadata.test.ts extensions/policy/src/doctor/register.test.ts extensions/policy/src/cli.test.ts src/commands/doctor-lint.test.ts --reporter=dot` passed: 4 files, 329 tests.\n- `pnpm tsgo:extensions` passed.\n- `pnpm exec oxfmt --check src/flows/health-checks.ts extensions/policy/src/doctor/register.ts extensions/policy/src/doctor/register.test.ts extensions/policy/src/doctor/fix-metadata.ts extensions/policy/src/doctor/metadata.test.ts extensions/policy/src/cli.ts extensions/policy/src/cli.test.ts src/commands/doctor-lint.ts src/commands/doctor-lint.test.ts` passed.\n- `pnpm exec oxlint src/flows/health-checks.ts extensions/policy/src/doctor/register.ts extensions/policy/src/doctor/register.test.ts extensions/policy/src/doctor/fix-metadata.ts extensions/policy/src/doctor/metadata.test.ts extensions/policy/src/cli.ts extensions/policy/src/cli.test.ts src/commands/doctor-lint.ts src/commands/doctor-lint.test.ts` passed.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD && git diff --check` passed.\n\n## Stack\n\nRestacked directly onto current `openclaw/openclaw@main` after #99121 merged. Current PR head: `2466c7a3f21afc82848df02ef25886ac0177319b`.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n\nBehavior or issue addressed:\nPolicy doctor findings expose structured `fixRecommendation` metadata in public JSON output for current policy check ids while attestation output remains recommendation-free.\n\nReal environment tested:\nWSL Ubuntu root checkout `/root/src/openclaw-workflow/.worktrees/pr-99686` on restacked head `2466c7a3f21afc82848df02ef25886ac0177319b`, with an isolated temp workspace under `/tmp/openclaw-policy-fix-proof.*`. The temp config enabled the source policy plugin, set the default agent workspace to the temp directory, enabled the Telegram channel, and authored a `policy.jsonc` deny rule for provider `telegram`. No live LLM or network provider calls were made.\n\nExact steps or command run after this patch:\n1. `OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH=/tmp/openclaw-policy-fix-proof.*/openclaw.jsonc node scripts/run-node.mjs --dev doctor --lint --json --only policy/channels-denied-provider`\n2. `OPENCLAW_CONFIG_PATH=/tmp/openclaw-policy-fix-proof.*/openclaw.jsonc node --import tsx --eval 'import(\"./extensions/policy/src/cli.ts\").then(async ({policyCheckCommand}) => { process.exitCode = await policyCheckCommand({ cwd: process.env.PROOF_DIR, json: true }); })'`\n\nEvidence after fix:\n`doctor --lint --json` exited `1` as expected for the seeded policy violation and emitted this finding:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"checkId\": \"policy/channels-denied-provider\",\n  \"severity\": \"error\",\n  \"message\": \"Channel 'telegram' uses denied provider 'telegram'.\",\n  \"source\": \"policy\",\n  \"path\": \"openclaw config\",\n  \"ocPath\": \"oc://openclaw.config/channels/telegram\",\n  \"target\": \"oc://openclaw.config/channels/telegram\",\n  \"requirement\": \"oc://policy.jsonc/channels/denyRules/#0\",\n  \"fixHint\": \"Disable this channel, remove it from config, or update the policy deny rule.\",\n  \"fixRecommendation\": {\n    \"fixClass\": \"automatic\",\n    \"policyPath\": [\"channels\", \"denyRules\"],\n    \"configTargets\": [\"channels\"],\n    \"summary\": \"Disable product-managed channels matching the denied provider.\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThe supplemental policy check JSON path also exited `1`, emitted the same `fixRecommendation`, and kept the attestation object to hashes/paths only:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"attestation\": {\n    \"policy\": { \"path\": \"policy.jsonc\", \"hash\": \"sha256:f7bea32f53401bb152a32836107514220ab6282b5f5c7149787f4c5ee3c685bb\" },\n    \"workspace\": { \"scope\": \"policy\", \"hash\": \"sha256:a03faac8463be7dbad38177af758315a5d39438a2e338118fa1a847adb93ac36\" },\n    \"findingsHash\": \"sha256:66792d3024b94eeea5769cb13fc07cebad84247704006fa05928741676011936\",\n    \"attestationHash\": \"sha256:8ba8818628c7e36a6b76e5fa5692fe1ba88923b3530c7ad64c540a42dcea0cf7\"\n  },\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"checkId\": \"policy/channels-denied-provider\",\n      \"fixRecommendation\": {\n        \"fixClass\": \"automatic\",\n        \"policyPath\": [\"channels\", \"denyRules\"],\n        \"configTargets\": [\"channels\"],\n        \"summary\": \"Disable product-managed channels matching the denied provider.\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nObserved result after fix:\nBoth public JSON paths expose `fixRecommendation` on the policy finding, and the policy attestation remains recommendation-free. The branch is no longer stacked on #99121 in Git history; the PR diff is now 9 files directly against current `main`.\n\nWhat was not tested:\nNo packaged release binary, live provider run, or live LLM call was run. The `policy check --json` proof used the source command implementation because this source checkout's top-level `--dev` CLI did not preload the policy plugin command, while `doctor --lint --json` used the actual CLI launcher.\n",
